{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>First interpretation</b><br>שררך. It is the navel [like רפאות תהי לשרך]." "אגן. Round, like באגנות." "הסהר. [Targum] moon [סיהרא], like הסהרונים [and so in the language of Ishmael]." "המזג. In the language of the Rabbis it is known [like מסכה יינה]." "סוגה. Also in their language, a fence." "<b>Second interpretation</b><br>שררך. Girded with a belt and a precious stone, round like the moon, that it not lack; and on this interpretation המזג will be in a different sense." "בטנך. It looks like a heap of wheat, which is thick below [and thin above], and the meaning of סוגה בשושנים is the red garment [for it says דתמר, for the heap would not have been visible, for שושנים surround it]." "<b>Third interpretation</b><br>שררך. The Great Sanhedrin, likened to half a circular threshing floor." "אל יחסר המזג. This is the Torah, which is likened to wine." "בטנך ערמת חטים. The Lesser Sanhedrin." "סוגה בשושנים. The majority of the righteous."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:54.823174167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}